comment: The concept of “breed reported in geographic location by FAO National Coordinators” is unique to DAD-IS (https://www.fao.org/dad-is/en/). This VBO term should therefore be used specifically for the breed conforming to this concept.
synonym: "Danish Red Cattle" EXACT [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
synonym: "Red Danish Dairy Cattle" EXACT [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
synonym: "Rød Dansk Malkerace anno 1970 (RDM-1970)" EXACT most_common_name [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
is_a: VBO:0000191 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! Danish Red (Cattle)
is_a: VBO:0400000 {source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153", source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648"} ! Vertebrate breed
relationship: VBO:0300020 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q35 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! breed reported in geographic location
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5520-6597
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965
property_value: dcterms:source "https://www.fao.org/dad-is" xsd:anyURI
property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "In the 1840s, original cattle on the Eastern Danish islands were crossed with red cattle from the Southern part of Denmark. Three groups of cattle were used: Angler Cattle, Northern Slesviger Cattle and Ballum Cattle. The resulting cattle was the foundation for the Red Danish Dairy Cattle, RDM, officially formed in 1878. The RDM was most popular in the 1950s but it has decreased a lot since then. From the late 1970s the breed association introduced breeding material from other breeds, e.g. Brown-Swiss, Red Holstein and Swedish Red, into the RDM. Only a small fraction of the breeders continued pure-breeding after this, and they formed \"RDM-1970\". Subsequently, a small group of breeders formed the \"RDM-1930\" - a slightly different line. Both lines represent the original Red Danish Dairy Cattle." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

