property_value: origindescription "imported; locally adapted; The Jersey breed originated on the Island of Jersey, a small British island in the English Channel off the coast of France. The Jersey is one of the oldest dairy breeds, having been reported by authorities as being purebred for nearly six centuries." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

