property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "In the 16TH century, Portuguese explorers reported the presence of cattle in present day Zimbabwe, and the first White settlers found large numbers of an estimated 500,000 cattle in the hands of the local inhabitants.nThese were distributed along the central plateau, which was a Tsetse fly free zone, and were almost exclusively of the SANGA type.n" xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

