property_value: origindescription "Studies on crossbreeding of cattle were embarked on in 1930s at Mpwapwa. Several Bos indicus (Tanzania Shorthorn Zebu, Boran, Sahiwal and Red Sindhi) and Bos taurus (Ayrshire, Friesian, Jersey and Guernsey) were involved. These studies led to the development of the composite Mpwapwa Breed of which 75% constitutes of Sahiwal and Red Sindhi." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

