property_value: origindescription "Variety (with coloured reduced to a few spots on side) of Polish Marsh. Whitebacked cattle originate from aurochs Bos primigenius. It is found in the region from the Narwia river, through the Bug river basin, to the Wieprz river. In the middle of the 20th century it was considered extinct. When few individuals were found, working on restitution of the original population began." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

