property_value: origindescription "imported; Simmental cattle are a Swiss breed, which originated under the conditions of the lush Alpine pastures. The extinct Kula Cattle was the first simmentalized breed in our country. It was developed in North-Western Bulgaria by random crossing of the local gray cattle with Simmental bulls, mainly of Serbian and Swiss origin. At a later stage, the Bulgarian Simmental Cattle breed was created by reproductive and assimilative crossing." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

