property_value: origindescription "The breed was developed by continuous (40-50 years) random crossing of the local gray cattle from Northwest Bulgaria with Simmental bulls of Swiss and Yugoslavian origin. Thus, the Kulsko Cattle was developed. At a later stage the Bulgarian Simmental Cattle breed was developed by reproductive crossing of the Kulsko and Gray Iskar Cattle breeds, and systematic and purposeful breeding improvement work." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

