property_value: origindescription "indigenous breed. Belongs to the family of the European short horn cattle (Bos brachyceros europeus, Ruetimeyer). Today's Busa was probably created by crossbreeding the indigenous breed brachiceros cattle and shorthorn cattle brought by migrating peoples from the Northeast (Alpine brown, Tyrolean grey and Pinzgau cattle)." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

