property_value: origindescription "composite of Ghana Shorthorn and Zebu (White Fulani, sometimes Sokoto Gudali): Ghana Sanga is a more recent and specific cross compared to the general cattle group called Sanga and which comprises long term established zebu x humpless derivatives represented by several breeds in eastern Africa and southern Africa. The Ghana Sanga resembles the Shorthorn type more closely than does the zebu, but like the Zebu, it is found in drier areas of the country, towards the northern border and on the Accra plains extending into Volta Region." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

