property_value: origindescription "Istrian cattle in its phenotype is similar to podolian cattle whose ancient homeland is the area of Podolia and Volhinia from where it spread to the larger part of Panonia, and along the Adriatic Coast to South Europe and North Africa. At the end of the 18th century a targeted introduction of podolian primigen Italian breeds from Romagna, Puglia, Marcha and Polesina was made." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

