property_value: origindescription "The breed is named as √¢‚Ç¨ÀúNari√¢‚Ç¨‚Ñ¢ by the community. √¢‚Ç¨ÀúNari√¢‚Ç¨‚Ñ¢ is derived from the word √¢‚Ç¨ÀúNar√¢‚Ç¨‚Ñ¢ which means hills. Majority of the Nari cattle population are found surrounding the Aravali forest range in Sirohi and Pali districts of Rajasthan andBanaskanth, Sabarkantha districts of Gujarat. These regions are slightly hilly and undulating and can be described as native tract of Nari cattle" xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

