property_value: origindescription "Breeding the Oravka hen started in the 50ies of the 20th century. Native hens from the Slovak territory (Zakamenne, Novot) were used as the basic breeding material. They were crossbred with the Wyandotte, Rhode Island Red and New Hampshire breeds. The breed is considered as Slovak national breed." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

