property_value: origindescription "indigenous :Bobthra is the most common line of indigenous chicken found in Bhutan. Many farmers believe they are the immediate descendant of the jungle fowl and for this reason, male and female of this line are collectively called Bobthra (Dz). They are also called Bja Katseri due to its high resemblance to red jungle fowl." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

