property_value: origindescription "The Tai Lake basin had the traditions of rearing chicken as early as in Zhou dynasty, it had became common from the Spring-Autumn period to the Han Empire and prosperous in the late Qing dynasty to early republic. The rich products of the Tai Lake basin and living habits of local people promote the formation of this breed." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

