property_value: origindescription "This breed originated in the G√É¬¢tinais region, between Montargis, Sens, Seine-et-Marne and Loiret (France). The crossing of local stock with White Brahma resulted in the Gatinaise in the 19th century or earlier. This breed is considered as well as the Gauloise Doree as the national French emblem. It has been known for time immemorial in the G√É¬¢tinais region." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

