property_value: origindescription "These are common fowls of Tuscany country-side, named after the port of Livorno, from where the first specimen of the white variety reached America (1829-30) and, later, England and Denmark. In the above listed countries, the Livorno breed, then became Leghorn, was selected for both egg production (white variety) and plumage colour (13 different varieties)." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

