property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "In the late 19th century, indigenous chicken in the Nagoya area were crossed with Buff Cochins and other imported breeds. The cross-breds were upgraded for egg production. Until the 1950s, cross-breds of Nagoya and White Leghorn were widely used as layers. Recently, it has been noticed that the meat of this breed is very good in quality, and the cross-breds of Nagoya and meat type chicken are now used for broiler production." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

