[Term]
id: VBO:0007824
name: Phuphan black bone 2 chicken, Thailand (Chicken)
comment: The concept of “breed reported in geographic location by FAO National Coordinators” is unique to DAD-IS (https://www.fao.org/dad-is/en/). This VBO term should therefore be used specifically for the breed conforming to this concept.
synonym: "Phuphan black bone 2 chicken" EXACT most_common_name [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
is_a: NCBITaxon:9031 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! Gallus gallus
is_a: VBO:0400000 {source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153", source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648"} ! Vertebrate breed
relationship: VBO:0300020 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q869 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! breed reported in geographic location
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5520-6597
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965
property_value: dcterms:source "https://www.fao.org/dad-is" xsd:anyURI
property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "Phuphan black bone 2 chicken originated during the development of Phuphan black bone 1 chicken. During generation 3 and 4, some chick had white feather. But the baby weight is smaller. Phuphan Royal Livestock Education and Development Center, they had collected white feather black bone chicken and established new line. They used line breeding and selection. They have white feather, black eye, black beak, black skinned, black meat and black bone. It is resistant to the environment and epidemic. They are raised for 3-4 months and sent to slaughter house. In females, the average egg production is 80-100 eggs / year. They have unique peanut or black rose crested. The carcass is black with high level of carnosine as an antioxidant." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

[Term]
id: VBO:0007825
name: Pradu Hang dum, Thailand (Chicken)
comment: The concept of “breed reported in geographic location by FAO National Coordinators” is unique to DAD-IS (https://www.fao.org/dad-is/en/). This VBO term should therefore be used specifically for the breed conforming to this concept.
synonym: "Pradu Hang dum" EXACT most_common_name [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
is_a: NCBITaxon:9031 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! Gallus gallus
is_a: VBO:0400000 {source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153", source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648"} ! Vertebrate breed
relationship: VBO:0300020 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q869 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! breed reported in geographic location
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5520-6597
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965
property_value: dcterms:source "https://www.fao.org/dad-is" xsd:anyURI
property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "Pradu Hang Dam chicken is Thai indigenous chicken. They are developed from cockroaches. They are developed together with Lueng Hang Khao chicken. They were known in the Sukhothai period. They were brought to be fighting cocks that was popular sport in that period. Pradu Hang Dam chicken was a traditional breed that is popular in Suphanburi, Ang Thong, Ayutthaya, Chachoengsao, Min Buri and Nong Chok. These area are the good source of this chicken. Pradu Hang Dam chicken is a medium size chicken. (Male, BW = 3 kg, Female, BW = 2 kg.) Egg shell color is light brown." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

