property_value: origindescription "imported; The original stock of Rusa was introduced from New South Wales from New Caledonia between 1861 and 1885. The original stock of Rusa was the Javan race - a smaller subspecies, the Moluccan rusa, is located on some of the offshore islands north of the mainland. Liberations were made in New South Wales, Victoria and Western Australia with the surviving population centred around Sydney's Royal National Park and its surroundings." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

