property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "In Hongwu years of Ming Dynasty, Pingba gray geese were introduced into the producing area by station troops whose native place was Fengyang of Anhui Province. Local people have the custom of using gray geese as sacrifice. Furthermore, there are many Hui people in the producing area, and geese are their main meat food. Thus, Pingba gray geese were formed after long-term acclimatization and artificial selection." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

