property_value: origindescription "Created through cross-breeding warm-blood mare with imported studs of (and other cold-blood breeds. Systematic breeding started in the first half of 19th century. Due to different establishment stock of mares and different studs of cold blood breeds present in the area of Croatia accompanied with environment factors of a certain area, Croatian cold blood is a fairly heterogeneous population when it comes to phenotype." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

