property_value: origindescription "The Posavje horse breed originated on the basis of the autochthonous horses reared on the bank of Sava River, mostly in Posavje. Those horses were improved with different breeds, mostly with coldblooded breeds of Belgian coldblooded type. The breed is traditionally reared in Slovenia at Posavje region, mostly at Kr√Ö¬°ko polje and Bre√Ö¬æice region. The Posavinje horse is reared also in Croatia." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

