property_value: origindescription "The breed was developed at the begining of the century at the Tori breeding station (originally developed for Estonian native horses). Composite of Estonian, Hackney (1896-1926) cross-bred with Breton Posthorse (till 1970) and Hannover (recent years) it has also some influence from other breeds such as Norfolk, East Friesian and Holstein. At present the main breeding goal is a lighter horse type." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

