property_value: dcterms:source "https://www.fao.org/dad-is" xsd:anyURI
property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "Thapra Muscovy Duck (Pedted Thapra) Thapra Muscovy Duck (Pedted Thapra) was developed by Thapra Livestock Research and Breeding Center, Department of Livestock development. The objective was to improve growth and reproductive traits of Thai Native duck. In 1983, they were collected from 8 provinces in Northeastern part of Thailand. They were improved genetics by crossing with Muscovy duck originated from South Africa. Eggs of duck were increased from 77 to 98 eggs per year. Now egg production trait is 180 eggs/year." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

