property_value: origindescription "The foundation stock consisted of pigs bought from Poles resettlings in the Olsztyn province after moving from the Vilnus and Nowogrodczyzna regions. These pigs were crosses between primitive local long-eared and short-eared pigs. Selected for fat-meat type. Zlotniki Spotted is maintained in few herds in the north-west and central Poland." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

