property_value: origindescription "indigenous breed- The existence of the local pig breeds is also quite interesting.National survey findings indicate that local pig breeds existed since generations and their ancestors could be the wild boar.This is because some of the physical characteristics are very closely related to the wild boar.Farmers have been rearing this breed since the time of their great grand-parents.There is a spatial distribution of native pigs across Bhutan.Looking at the potential pockets areas across the regions,it indicates that a larger concentration of native pigs is located in western and west- central Bhutan compared to Eastern and East Central Bhutan." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

