[Term]
id: VBO:0013200
name: krskopolje, Slovenia (Pig)
comment: The concept of “breed reported in geographic location by FAO National Coordinators” is unique to DAD-IS (https://www.fao.org/dad-is/en/). This VBO term should therefore be used specifically for the breed conforming to this concept.
synonym: "krskopolje" EXACT most_common_name [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
synonym: "Krskopolje pig" EXACT [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
synonym: "Krskopoljski prasic" EXACT [] {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
is_a: NCBITaxon:9823 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! Sus scrofa
is_a: VBO:0017222 {source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965"} ! Krskopolje (Pig)
is_a: VBO:0400000 {source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153", source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648"} ! Vertebrate breed
relationship: VBO:0300020 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q215 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"} ! breed reported in geographic location
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5520-6597
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965
property_value: dcterms:source "https://www.fao.org/dad-is" xsd:anyURI
property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "The first known written record dates from the middle of 19th century. Rohrman (1899) prepared a detailed description of breed in Kmetijske novice and he also named the breed as Kr√Ö¬°kopolje pig. He stressed that pigs in the area of Kr√Ö¬°ko field are uniform in exterior, color, and also in other traits, and that they are distinguishable from other breeds. However, many breeders from that time mixed and crossed the Kr√Ö¬°kopolje pig with Yorkshire. In the rural survey from the year 1938, Oblak pointed out that the original Kr√Ö¬°kopolje pig can be found only in the most distant villages. After the Second World War, many studies in fertility, fattening and meatiness of Kr√Ö¬°kopolje pig was performed (Eiselt and Ferjan, 1972). On the other hand, breeders were left to themselves without any professional support at breeding and rearing. The breed was put to the list of endangered Slovenian breeds in the year 1991. The herdbook was established in the 1992. Three family farms were included in gene bank and they started with pedigree and performance recording." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

