property_value: origindescription "Ca. 1900, the white variety of \"Danish rabbit\" and Belgian Giant were crossed by the head of Copenhagen Zoo, Julius Schi√É¬∏tt, to produce a large albino rabbit - Hvid Dansk Landkanin. This breed was displayed for the first time at a show in Tivoli, Copenhagen in 1908. In the 1950s and 1960s, the breed was very popular, and thousands of animals were exported for breeding in England, Germany, Hungary and Switzerland." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

