property_value: origindescription "Swiniarka is an old primitive breed kept in Poland for centuries. It was considered extinct in the second half of the 20th century. After 1985, a small number of Swiniarka sheep was found in different part of the country and then bought, enabling conservation of the breed. Nowadays this breed is kept in one flock near Kielce." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

