property_value: origindescription "Corriedale sheep was developed in Australia and New Zealand by extensive breeding and culling as a cross between Merino and Lincoln sheep. The goal was to develop a breed that would thrive in lower rainfall areas and supply long staple wool. The breed was developed between 1868 and 1930 (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corriedale)." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

