property_value: origindescription "Karakul is one of the ancient breed. It was introduced to the territory of Uzbekistan long time ago using national breeding methods . Some specific and original groups of animals connected each other are presented in this breed. It includes sheep of 15 colourations, 30 colours, 4 wool constitutional curl types and more than 20 types and curl forms. Genetic fund of the breed is enriched 24 productive pedigree types of karakul sheeps with variuos colours and colourations." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

