property_value: origindescription "The breed was resulted in crossing of local fine-fleece dams with Lincoln and Romney-Marsh rams. This crossing resulted in big rams and rather small poll ewes. Crosses were bred pure and selected for two types: √ê¬ê (Romney-Marsh descendents) - finefleeced, with dense, but not too much long (up to 9.5 cm) wool and B-type, which was characterised with less qualitative wool, but which was longer and more technological. Since 1952 improving of breed is done for type B." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

