property_value: hasdomesticationstatus VBO:0300007 {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}
property_value: origindescription "The development of the Poll Merino is relatively new. Recessive poll genes are believed to have existed in the breed for many years and infusions of hornless sheep during the development of the Merino breed in Australia also left some poll genes within normal Merino flocks. Poll rams have been selected and mated to Merino ewes and selection continued for the quality of polledness. The result is a pure Merino without horns." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

