property_value: origindescription "Albanian researchers classify Shkodrane breed in the group of √¢‚Ç¨≈ìCakel√¢‚Ç¨¬ù sheep breed , whose ancestor should be looked for in the domesticated populations of Far East. Until the end of first half of last century , this breed had been dominant in over and sub Shkodra areas. After 1965√¢‚Ç¨‚Ñ¢s , especially 1970-80√¢‚Ç¨‚Ñ¢s this breed submitted crosses with the imported Cigaja and Merino breeds. A part of population was crossed with other autochthonous breed √¢‚Ç¨≈ìBardhoka√¢‚Ç¨¬ù." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

