property_value: origindescription "composite of Wiltshire Horn,Border Leicester, Poll Dorset and Poll Merino sheep. Requirements for registration of Wiltipoll sheep state that the sheep must have no less than 96.87% Wiltshire Horn blood. To achieve the required percentage of Wiltshire Horn blood, a ewe of a polled breed must be first crossed with a pure bred Wiltshire Horn ram and then back -crossed successively for four generations." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

