property_value: origindescription "indigenous breed . In Merak-Sakten (Eastern Bhutan), the oral history seems to trace their origin to Tsona in south-east Tibet. It was stated that the present day residents of Merak-Sakten migrated with their yaks and sheep to avoid the wrath of their local ruler.The time of their migration could be dated to 7th century during the era the famous king Srongtsen Gampo (Wangmo, undated)." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

