property_value: origindescription "composite of Shropshire (and Pr√É¬©coce) and Kazakh Fat-Rumped. It is the unique, rare breed, combining the semi-fine fleece with a fat rump. It has been bred for several decades. First experiments were started in 1914: Kazakh fat-rumped female sheep were crossed with English Shropshire meat semi-fine-fleece breed rams. The introductory crossing with precos, the offspring of fat-rumped females and preco rams, was also applied." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

