property_value: origindescription "The Churra da Terra Quente breed, formerly also known as 'Tarrincha' or 'Terrincha', is a breed of recent name and characterisation, but its genesis dates back to the late 19th and early 20th centuries, when animals of the Churra Badana and Churra Mondegueira breeds began to cross with each other, thus obtaining an animal with zootechnical attributes well suited to its area of exploitation and more productive." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

