property_value: origindescription "The original population of turkeys was imported from Bosnia in the 18th century. Later they mixed with the imported Bronze turkey, which resulted in the Copper turkey breed. The pure-bred population is now considered as Hungarian indigenous breed." xsd:string {source="https://www.fao.org/dad-is"}

