[Term]
id: VBO:0200986
name: Random-Bred Dog (Dog)
def: "A dog that has no known or obvious ancestry from a recognized breed." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5520-6597, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965]
comment: Random-bred dogs are common in both rural and urban environments, and are often called village or street dogs, mongrels, mutts, native dogs or pariah dogs. Having no known or obvious breed ancestry distinguishes them from mixed breed dogs which, as the name implies, are animals that are known or appear to be a mixture of two or more breeds.
synonym: "Mongrel" EXACT [] {source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5520-6597", source="http://omia.org", source="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9178-3965"}
