[Term]
id: VBO:0201393
name: obsolete Walker Hound (Dog)
comment: Merged terms Walker Hound and Treeing Walker Coonhound. Walker hounds are a strain of American foxhound derived from the English foxhound. Walker hounds are used to hunt bear and other large game and generally hunt in large numbers (15-20 or more) in a pack. PMID:1783305 https://wagwalking.com/breed/treeing-walker-coonhound; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treeing_Walker_Coonhound.
