[Typedef]
id: VBO:0300019
name: has foundation stock
def: "A relation between two distinct material entities (breeds or species), a descendant entity and an ancestor entity, in which the descendant entity is the result of mating, manipulation, or geographical or cultural isolation of the ancestor entity, therefore inheriting some of the ancestor’s genetic material." []
comment: A "foundation stock" refers to animals that are the progenitors, or foundation, of a breed or of a given bloodline within such. Many modern breeds can be traced to specific, named foundation animals, but a group of animals may be referred to collectively as foundation bloodstock when one distinct population (including both landrace breeds or a group of animals linked to a deliberate and specific selective breeding program) provides part of the underlying genetic base for a new distinct population. (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foundation_stock.) Example of usage: 'Cymric (cat)' (VBO:0100080) has foundation stock 'Manx (cat)' (VBO:0100156).
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648
property_value: dcterms:created "2024-04-11T14:49:29Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000116 "has foundation stock can be used to relate a breed to one or more other breeds, or to a \"species\" (ie an NCBITaxon term) as in the cases of \"hybrid breeds\". \"Hybrid breeds\" are created by crossing animals of different species." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/monarch-initiative/vertebrate-breed-ontology/issues/209" xsd:anyURI
domain: NCBITaxon:7742 ! Vertebrata <vertebrates>
is_transitive: true

[Typedef]
id: VBO:0300020
name: breed reported in geographic location
def: "A relation between a breed and the geographic location where the breed was reported to exist by country-nominated FAO National Coordinators." []
comment: Officially nominated FAO National Coordinators report breeds existing in their country (these breeds are reported in the DAD-IS breed list). 'breed reported in geographic location' refers to the region where the breed was reported. For example: VBO:0007427 represents the 'Alatau' breed reported to be found in Kyrgyzstan by the FAO coordinators.
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: dcterms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648
property_value: dcterms:created "2024-11-05T18:13:40Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/monarch-initiative/vertebrate-breed-ontology/issues/209" xsd:anyURI

